WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:20.298
The first thing I had to do at school was get permission to use my new invention.

2
00:00:20.299 --> 00:00:24.416
Luckily, Mrs. Romano thought it sounded like a great idea.

3
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:28.589
So did Mr. Dalmati, the recess helper.

4
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:33.883
At recess all the kids came running out and got in line for the slide.

5
00:00:33.884 --> 00:00:39.446
Josh, Molly, and I ran over with the two shopping bags.

6
00:00:39.447 --> 00:00:43.736
"Pick a number for the slide!" called Josh.

7
00:00:43.737 --> 00:00:46.882
"Then grab a toy!"

8
00:00:46.883 --> 00:00:50.843
"What are the numbers for?" asked one little girl.

9
00:00:50.844 --> 00:00:55.391
"It's to hold your place in line for the slide," I explained.

10
00:00:55.392 --> 00:00:59.125
"You can take a toy too," Molly added.

11
00:00:59.126 --> 00:01:01.955
"When your number is called, turn in your toy.

12
00:01:01.956 --> 00:01:05.275
Then you don't have to wait in line for the slide."

13
00:01:05.276 --> 00:01:08.320
"Cool!" said a fifth-grade boy.

14
00:01:08.321 --> 00:01:11.540
"That sounds like fun!"

15
00:01:11.541 --> 00:01:16.173
Josh handed out the numbers, and I gave out the toys.

16
00:01:16.174 --> 00:01:20.790
Pretty soon we were out of numbers and out of toys.

17
00:01:20.791 --> 00:01:26.392
"Numbers one, two, and three, line up!" called Josh.

18
00:01:26.393 --> 00:01:29.325
Three kids ran over to us.

19
00:01:29.326 --> 00:01:32.526
They handed in their numbers along with their toys.

20
00:01:32.527 --> 00:01:36.045
Then they climbed up to the slide.

21
00:01:36.046 --> 00:01:39.927
You would not believe how great my invention worked!

22
00:01:39.928 --> 00:01:42.504
All the kids loved it.

23
00:01:42.505 --> 00:01:47.118
They traded toys and ran around, laughing and playing.

24
00:01:47.119 --> 00:01:51.075
Everyone stopped pushing and shoving in line.

25
00:01:51.076 --> 00:01:54.000
In fact, there was no line.

26
00:01:54.001 --> 00:02:01.790
We only called out three numbers at a time, so kids got to go on the slide without waiting for very long.

27
00:02:01.791 --> 00:02:07.601
I felt proud to see my Pick-a-Number invention working so well.

28
00:02:07.602 --> 00:02:11.043
Mr. Dalmati was happy too.

29
00:02:11.044 --> 00:02:14.481
"Great idea, Iggy," he told me.

30
00:02:14.482 --> 00:02:17.506
"You solved a big recess problem."

31
00:02:17.507 --> 00:02:20.357
A first-grade girl ran over to me.

32
00:02:20.358 --> 00:02:25.620
"This number game is so much fun!" she said.

33
00:02:25.621 --> 00:02:28.959
"Can we play it again tomorrow?"

34
00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.639
"We can play it whenever we have outdoor recess," I said.

35
00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:39.125
The kids loved the number game almost as much as they loved the slide!

36
00:02:39.126 --> 00:02:44.774
After recess I wrote about my Pick-a-Number invention for Mr. Bright.

37
00:02:44.775 --> 00:02:48.035
Then I handed my paper to Mrs. Romano.

38
00:02:48.036 --> 00:02:50.596
She put it with the other ideas.

39
00:02:50.597 --> 00:02:55.080
Everything was working out just the way I had hoped.

40
00:02:55.081 --> 00:03:00.259
But there was one thing that still bothered me—Jenny.

41
00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.375
She didn't take a turn calling out numbers.

42
00:03:03.376 --> 00:03:05.951
She said it wasn't any fun.

43
00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:11.442
Not only that, but she got a "D" on her math test that day.

44
00:03:11.443 --> 00:03:15.081
She told me about it on the way home from school.

45
00:03:15.082 --> 00:03:20.111
"I studied really hard," she said with tears in her eyes.

46
00:03:20.112 --> 00:03:22.446
"I just don't know what's wrong!

47
00:03:22.447 --> 00:03:26.221
My dad is going to be so upset."

48
00:03:26.222 --> 00:03:29.855
If only I could think of a way to help her!

49
00:03:29.856 --> 00:03:35.011
"Sara is having trouble in school too," Jenny blurted out.

50
00:03:35.012 --> 00:03:41.139
She sighed. "At least I'm not the only one."

51
00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:42.447
I looked at her.

52
00:03:42.448 --> 00:03:45.398
"How do you know that?" I asked.

53
00:03:45.399 --> 00:03:50.538
Sara was Jenny's friend, the one who had just moved to another neighborhood.

54
00:03:50.539 --> 00:03:55.091
"I talked to Sara last night on the phone," Jenny explained.

55
00:03:55.092 --> 00:03:57.886
"She told me she failed a reading test.

56
00:03:57.887 --> 00:04:01.204
It was her first test at her new school.

57
00:04:01.205 --> 00:04:06.232
She's worried everyone will think she's dumb."

58
00:04:06.233 --> 00:04:11.817
That night, when I went to bed, I was still thinking about Jenny's problem.

59
00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:15.273
I lay there, looking up through the skylight.

60
00:04:15.274 --> 00:04:19.501
Sometimes, if it's a clear night, I can see the stars.

61
00:04:19.502 --> 00:04:23.416
I imagine that they are winking just for me, Iggy.

62
00:04:23.417 --> 00:04:28.290
I pretend they're my friends, helping me to think of bright ideas.

63
00:04:28.291 --> 00:04:32.642
That night the stars looked clear and sharp.

64
00:04:32.643 --> 00:04:37.223
They winked, as though they were trying to tell me something.

65
00:04:37.224 --> 00:04:43.598
But what were they trying to tell me?
